  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Visitors, contributors, and volunteers can give optional feedback about finding goods, understanding claims, and managing the event.\", \"decision\": \"How should organizers learn which parts of the fair need improvement?\", \"goal\": \"Help usable household goods reach interested neighbors while keeping contributions, claims, and final collection understandable.\", \"problem\": \"Neighbors are organizing a one-day fair for clean, usable household goods that people no longer need. Giving and taking are both optional, and no payment or matching contribution is required. Volunteers have intake space, category tables, reserve shelves, a holding area, carts, and simple item records. Contributors choose in advance whether unclaimed goods should be returned during the closing collection period or donated through an arranged pickup.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nOrganizers place a short feedback card at the exit for visitors, contributors, and volunteers to complete before leaving. Fresh experiences are captured through the same questions, making recurring difficulties easier to recognize across different roles.\nOrganizers hold brief separate conversations with visitors, contributors, and volunteers, then compare notes about the fair’s main routines. Each group can explain problems in its own terms before organizers identify changes that would help more than one role.\nOrganizers send a short follow-up form after the fair and review responses alongside the recorded movement of goods. People have time to reflect, and their comments can be compared with practical information about what arrived and left."
    }
  ],
